WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0071: hats follow the head.

A rigid mesh alone in its visual that sits above the figure's waist in the figure's own space (a
hat) borrows the skin of the nearest skinned mesh of its figure, as the elf ears borrow the head's.

--- a/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_tav.rs
+++ b/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_tav.rs
@@ -511,18 +511,42 @@
 /// A rigid mesh in a visual that also has skinned meshes (the elf ears in the head visual) is
 /// placed by BG3 with the visual's root transform but moves with a bone; it takes the skin of the
 /// nearest vertex of the visual's largest skinned mesh (same model space), and that mesh's
-/// palette. A rigid mesh alone in its visual (the greataxe) keeps its own world transform.
+/// palette. A rigid mesh alone in its visual (the greataxe) keeps its own world transform, unless it
+/// sits on the figure in the figure's own space (a hat, patch 0071: see below).
 fn borrow_skin(meshes: &mut [TavMesh]) {
     for i in 0..meshes.len() {
         if meshes[i].kind != 1 {
             continue;
         }
         let (part, figure) = (meshes[i].part, meshes[i].figure);
-        let Some(j) = (0..meshes.len())
+        let sibling = (0..meshes.len())
             .filter(|j| meshes[*j].kind == 0 && meshes[*j].part == part && meshes[*j].figure == figure)
-            .max_by_key(|j| meshes[*j].pos.len())
-        else {
-            continue;
+            .max_by_key(|j| meshes[*j].pos.len());
+        // Patch 0071: a rigid mesh alone in its visual that sits on the figure in its own model space (a
+        // hat: BG3 gives its object the figure's root transform and moves it with the head bone at render,
+        // so it floated over a turning, nodding head; a playtest report) takes the skin of the skinned
+        // mesh of its figure nearest to it, as the ears take the head's. A weapon or a shield is in its
+        // own space (its origin at the grip, far from where it hangs), so it keeps its own transform:
+        // only a mesh above the figure's waist (its lowest vertex at 0.9 m or more) whose centre is within
+        // HAT_REACH of a skinned vertex is borrowed.
+        const HAT_REACH: f32 = 0.35;
+        let j = match sibling {
+            Some(j) => j,
+            None => {
+                let m = &meshes[i];
+                if m.pos.is_empty() || m.pos.iter().map(|p| p.y).fold(f32::INFINITY, f32::min) < 0.9 {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                let c = m.pos.iter().copied().sum::<Vec3>() / m.pos.len() as f32;
+                let near = (0..meshes.len())
+                    .filter(|j| meshes[*j].kind == 0 && meshes[*j].figure == figure && meshes[*j].lod == m.lod)
+                    .filter_map(|j| meshes[j].pos.iter().map(|p| p.distance(c)).min_by(f32::total_cmp).map(|d| (j, d)))
+                    .min_by(|a, b| a.1.total_cmp(&b.1));
+                match near {
+                    Some((j, d)) if d <= HAT_REACH => j,
+                    _ => continue,
+                }
+            }
         };
         let (src_key, src_pos, src_w, src_b) =
             (meshes[j].key, meshes[j].pos.clone(), meshes[j].weights.clone(), meshes[j].bones.clone());
